{
  "manufacturer": "Endress+Hauser",
  "manufacturer_slug": "endress-hauser",
  "model": "Proline Prosonic Flow W 400 ultrasonic flowmeter (Modbus RS485)",
  "model_slug": "prosonic-flow-w-400-modbus",
  "short_model": "Prosonic Flow W 400",
  "aliases": [
    "Prosonic Flow W 400"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (clamp-on ultrasonic flowmeter)",
  "applies_to": "Proline Prosonic Flow W 400 clamp-on flowmeter with the Modbus RS485 output, as described in GP01207D/06/EN/01.24.",
  "summary": "The Prosonic Flow W 400 is Endress+Hauser's clamp-on ultrasonic time-of-flight flowmeter. Its Modbus RS485 interface gives every operating parameter a fixed register. This map covers what an integrator needs: flow, velocity, sound velocity, temperature, signal diagnostics, three totalizers and their controls, units, diagnostics and the Modbus settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "ASCII"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 247,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The manual prints registers in the Modbus Application Protocol form and equates them with Modicon 3XXXX/4XXXX numbers (its own example: 2007 = 32007); the scan-list parameter calls register addresses 1-based. Subtract 1 on the wire: volume flow at register 2007 is requested at 2006."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": "Valid from device firmware 01.00.zz",
  "source": {
    "title": "Description of Device Parameters Proline Prosonic Flow W 400 Modbus RS485",
    "doc_number": "GP01207D/06/EN/01.24-00",
    "revision_date": "2024-05-15",
    "url": "https://bdih-download.endress.com/file/005056A5E3831EEF84BF247676F6F971/GP01207DEN_0124-00.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 108-113 (Modbus settings, byte order), p. 174 (address model), pp. 190-206 (register tables)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Integrator subset of a parameter manual that lists a register for every menu item; installation (pipe/sensor), I/O, display, WLAN and web-server parameters are left out.",
    "Float word order follows the Byte order parameter (register 4915). The factory setting 1-0-3-2 sends byte 1, byte 0, byte 3, byte 2, byte 3 being sign and exponent, so floats are CDAB. Changing Byte order changes every float.",
    "Integer parameters are 2 bytes and listed as UINT16; the manual does not state signedness and all codes shown are positive.",
    "All parameters read with function 03 or 04 and write with 06 or 16; they are listed as holding registers.",
    "The no-parity picklist codes differ between the parameter description (2 = None/1 stop bit) and the register table (2 = None/2 stop bits), so only Even (0) and Odd (1) are given.",
    "The diagnostic registers return an integer whose coding the manual does not list.",
    "String parameters (tag, serial number, firmware, order code) and the scan list (5001-5016) are left out because their packing depends on the byte order setting.",
    "Velocity unit sits at register 2600, right next to the totalizer 1 block (2601 and up); do not confuse them.",
    "Non-volatile writes go to EEPROM; avoid cyclic writes.",
    "The data-bit and stop-bit count for the Even/Odd parity settings is not stated in this manual, so those defaults are left blank."
  ],
